{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show the 3D bamboo scene rendering properly in Chrome without blank screens or visual errors.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "OrbitControls sets `maxDistance = 45` without `maxPolarAngle`, allowing the camera to go below the ground (`y = -0.35`) and outside the bamboo grove (Screenshot 5 shows the camera zoomed outside the grove).",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "The scene uses two `InstancedMesh` calls (340 stalks, 3400 leaf planes), one 2048x2048 shadow map, and an `UnrealBloomPass`, which runs comfortably above 30 fps on integrated graphics.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 display a prominent UI bar (`#ui`) at the bottom left containing instructional text and three interactive buttons.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "In `animate()`, `windUniforms.uTime.value` updates automatically on load with `windOn = true`, driving vertex displacement in both `bambooMat` and `leafMat`.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 matches the reference photo's steep upward wide-angle perspective, converging foreground bamboo stalks, and dark overhanging branch on the upper left.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 show spacing and density of foreground and midground stalks comparable to the reference photo, though background depth falls off into white haze.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–3, heavy white bloom and fog wash out the deep greens and rich yellow-greens seen in the reference photo into pale, desaturated grey-greens.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "The reference photo looks straight up into the canopy and contains no visible ground elements, path, or brushwood fence; the 3D scene also lacks any path or fence (`CircleGeometry` ground plane).",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 reproduces the bright overhead sky illumination, though excessive bloom makes the scene much hazier and more overexposed than the crisp lighting in the photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 clearly show dark horizontal node rings with slight geometric bulges spaced at regular intervals along every bamboo stalk.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 and the instance scaling code (`scaleR = 0.68 + Math.random() * 0.55`, `scaleY = 0.82 + Math.random() * 0.32`) show varied stalk thicknesses and heights.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 show stalks leaning at varied natural angles, supported by randomized `rotation` and curved `CylinderGeometry` in the code.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 4 clearly shows the canopy composed of clusters of thin, narrow lanceolate leaves on twigs.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "In section 9 of the code, the ground is a flat, untextured `THREE.CircleGeometry(45, 48)` with a solid dark green `MeshStandardMaterial` (`color: 0x1a2616`) and no soil or fallen leaves.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 5 shows the entire circular patch of bamboo isolated in white fog with clear outer edges when zoomed out, and even in Screenshots 1–3 the perimeter is thin and blown out.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In the code, `leafInstanced` does not have `castShadow = true`, and Screenshots 1–3 show smooth uniform highlights along the stalks rather than dappled sunlight patches.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 show atmospheric bloom/haze (`FogExp2` and `UnrealBloomPass`) creating bright depth separation between foreground and background stalks.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show canopy leaves glowing with bright lime-green light against the sky, driven by `emissive` mapping and height-based color brightness.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show shaded areas on stalks and foliage retaining green ambient detail without crushing to pure black.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–3, the stalks exhibit a uniform, repetitive green gradient per segment and sharp specular streaks, lacking convincing natural yellowing, organic stains, or realistic waxy variation.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 4, leaf clusters appear as opaque, flat-shaded green cutouts (`alphaTest: 0.32` with uniform `emissive`) without true translucency or light transmission.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "The ground is an untextured solid-color `CircleGeometry` (`color: 0x1a2616`), which does not read as real soil, leaves, or stone.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 intentionally looks steeply upward so verticals converge, and the camera has no roll tilt (`camera.up` is default Y-up).",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "In `leafMat.onBeforeCompile`, vertex positions are displaced horizontally using `sin(uTime * ...)` for `canopySway` and `flutter`.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "In `bambooMat.onBeforeCompile`, horizontal wind displacement is multiplied by `pow(hFactor, 2.1)` where `hFactor = clamp(transformed.y / 28.0, 0.0, 1.0)`, bending tops much more than bases.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "In `bambooMat` and `leafMat`, wind motion uses fixed-amplitude continuous sine/cosine waves (`sin(uTime * 0.85 + phase) * 0.32 + sin(uTime * 1.9 + ...)`), lacking varied wind gusts over time.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "Neither the screenshots nor the HTML source code contain any particle systems, falling leaves, or drifting dust.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "In `animate()`, `uTime` advances continuously via `clock.getElapsedTime()` driving smooth, low-frequency sine functions (`0.85` and `0.72` rad/s) with no loop resets or jumps.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "Every stalk shares the exact same procedural texture (`bambooTex`) and geometry (`bambooGeo`), producing visibly identical dark node bands and pale rings across adjacent stalks in Screenshots 1–3.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "The code uses static instanced meshes without LOD switching, frustum-culling artifacts, or overlapping coplanar geometry, preventing pop-in or z-fighting flicker.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "In section 7 of the code, leaf planes (`PlaneGeometry(2.7, 2.7)`) are placed randomly around stalk coordinates (`anchor.x + (Math.random() - 0.5) * spread * 2.2`), causing flat leaf cards to intersect stalks as visible in Screenshot 4.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 looks distinctly synthetic due to the blown-out white background glow, harsh specular streaks on cylindrical stalks, flat dark tube branches, and on-screen UI.",
      "pass": false
    }
  ]
}
